.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH maw 1  "maw 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
maw \- declarative system manager for void linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaw\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
declarative system manager for void linux
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
maw\-init(1)
create a dotfiles repo, or adopt an existing one
.TP
maw\-build(1)
render changed modules into out/
.TP
maw\-activate(1)
build, then link everything into place
.TP
maw\-edit(1)
open a module, static dir, or config.nix (`config`) in $EDITOR, then activate
.TP
maw\-new(1)
create modules/<name>.nix, importing any live config, then edit it
.TP
maw\-add(1)
copy a file or dir into static/, then activate so it\*(Aqs linked back in place
.TP
maw\-diff(1)
show what activating would change in each live file
.TP
maw\-status(1)
everything out of sync: files, packages, services, and config for missing programs
.TP
maw\-adopt(1)
record installed packages and enabled services maw.nix doesn\*(Aqt know about
.TP
maw\-install(1)
install packages, record them in maw.nix, scaffold their modules, then activate
.TP
maw\-remove(1)
remove packages and drop them from maw.nix; their modules stay
.TP
maw\-query(1)
list packages you installed, or show one
.TP
maw\-search(1)
search xbps, or crates.io when xbps has nothing
.TP
maw\-info(1)
a package\*(Aqs details, and whether maw manages it
.TP
maw\-sync(1)
upgrade the system, then every unpinned cargo and go package
.TP
maw\-rollback(1)
restore a generation\*(Aqs repo and package versions, as a new generation
.TP
maw\-sv(1)
services: list, enable, disable, status, restart, log
.TP
maw\-generations(1)
list generations: each activation that changed something
.TP
maw\-commit(1)
commit every change in the repo
.TP
maw\-push(1)
push the repo to its remote
.TP
maw\-pull(1)
pull the repo from its remote, then activate
.TP
maw\-src(1)
packages built from your own xbps\-src templates in srcpkgs/
.TP
maw\-help(1)
read the docs: a topic, a command, or any section by its heading
.SH EXTRA
see: maw help
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBmaw-usage\fR(7), \fBmaw-migrating\fR(7), \fBmaw-modules\fR(5), \fBmaw-formats\fR(5)
